 ## Current release boundary
 
-Revision 92 implements `PERFBASE1`, the measurement-only baseline authority for the frozen campaign optimization program. It adds no scientific optimization and changes no TARGET-DATA2, training, evaluation, or GPU authority. Representative supplied LTA/replay and deterministic synthetic FEAS1/MVIDX1/MVSEL1 workloads are now content-addressed and measured across the serial, dual, bounded-intermediate, and automatic CPU schedules with exact output digests, timing, RSS, occupancy, throughput, and queue telemetry. The active qualification checkpoint is MACE-MPA-0 medium, but the PERFBASE1 schema is foundation-generic and remains valid for MACE-MH-1 campaigns. `TARGET-DATA2B-FEAS1-PERF3` remains the latest implemented runtime optimization; `PARCORE1` is the next optimization gate. GPU performance authority remains deferred.
+Revision 93 implements `PARCORE1`, the first runtime-optimization gate after the frozen `PERFBASE1` measurement authority. A reusable `DeterministicWorkQueue` now owns bounded work-conserving CPU dispatch, deterministic ordered reduction, task-identity failures, memory admission/backpressure, heartbeat telemetry, and locality metadata under `StageResourceScope`; FEAS1 is the first migrated consumer. FEAS1 neighborhood mathematics, canonical FP64 reduction order, TARGET-DATA2 records, training/evaluation semantics, and GPU authority are unchanged. The active qualification checkpoint remains MACE-MPA-0 medium, while the scheduler and evidence contracts contain no foundation-specific assumptions and remain valid for MACE-MH-1 campaigns. `PARCORE1` is the latest implemented runtime optimization; `NEIGHBOR1` is the next gate and will make FEAS1 and MVIDX1 share exact neighborhood production. GPU performance authority remains deferred.
